\tag{fdip}
\title{The relativistic scalar field}
\date{2026-11-09}

\p{The state now has controlled moments, a positive reflected form
and mixing. These are properties of Euclidean random distributions.
What Hilbert-space field do they determine, and what distinguishes
that field from a Gaussian or generalized free theory?}

